# spark-project-model Rules

These rules apply to `packages/spark-project-model/`.

## Model Direction

`ProjectModel` is the root model for software design plus runtime. Treat `ProjectModel` as the model subject; `ProjectEditor` is the shared editing collaboration layer for DevSystem and external automation.

Target mental model:

```text
ProjectModel
  design
  runtime
  editor
```

Current source layout remains:

```text
project/     ProjectModel
navigation/  ProjectNode, navigation DTOs, tree/flat transforms
page/        ConfigPageNode, PageNodeFactory, four-file content model
editor/      ProjectEditor facade and editor artifacts
infra/       file/navigation/reference/content loading
```

`src/MODEL-HIERARCHY.md` is the target model contract. `docs/unified-model-refactor-plan.md` is a future migration plan, not the current source map. Unless a task explicitly asks for directory migration, do not introduce planned paths such as `entity/`, `service/`, or `contract/` into imports, tests, or tooling.

## Boundaries

- Persistent source of truth remains DB navigation plus page files.
- `ProjectModel` may hold full headless runtime state, but runtime state must be traceable back to design source.
- `ProjectModel` must not directly hold Vue component instances, DOM nodes, Vue Router instances, Element Plus APIs, or browser globals as state.
- `ProjectEditor` serves human DevSystem editing and AI page-design with the same edit/CRUD/save/diagnostics flow.
- `ProjectEditor` must not become the model subject.
- Missing APIs, invalid config, unloaded pages, and inconsistent state must fail fast.

## Public Surface

Cross-package consumers may use only:

```text
@spark-appworks/spark-project-model
@spark-appworks/spark-project-model/project
```

Package-internal tests may target internal functions, but should import real current paths such as `../src/navigation/edit`.

## Verification

After implementation changes, run:

```bash
pnpm --dir packages/spark-project-model run typecheck
```

When touching editor, navigation, four-file models, or AI metadata, also run:

```bash
pnpm --dir packages/spark-project-model run test:run
```
